Execute a pre-defined mutation (write) skill.

Two-phase workflow:
    1. confirm=false (default) — validate + preview, no database changes;
        registers and returns a one-time preview_token
    2. confirm=true — verify and atomically consume preview_token.
        Managed single-statement Skills execute their cached plan
        directly in the framework without instantiating or calling
        the Skill class;
        imperative Skills re-validate and execute with conservative
        whole-operation outcome semantics.

For managed Skills, preview_sql and bound_params come from the same
cached plan and final binding used for execution. Skill-supplied
copies or unresolved values are rejected before token issuance.

Args:
    skill_name: The mutation skill name (e.g., "sample-update-order-status")
    params: Parameter dict matching the skill's frontmatter schema
    confirm: False=dry-run preview (default), True=actual execution
    preview_token: Required when confirm=True; returned by preview
    connection_id: Configured target connection; omit for the default

Returns:
    Preview result (confirm=false) or execution result (confirm=true).
    Every returned payload includes execution_outcome. Processable
    execute failures return success=false plus an extensible
    error_code with stable published meanings;
    callers must not infer success merely because no ToolError was
    raised and must never retry an unknown outcome automatically.

exec tool declaration:
```ts
declare const tools: { mcp__sql_safety_executor_mcp__execute_mutation_skill(args: {
  // False=preview (default), True=execute
  confirm?: boolean;
  // Connection alias. Pass exact aliases unchanged; omit only for default. Pass a resolved user/application target or unique db_type match explicitly. Use list_connections() to discover aliases or match a database type. For an unresolved purpose, ambiguous reference or irreconcilable scope restrictions, list candidates if needed, then ask and wait before database work. A default flag or successful check is not target selection. Omission never means all connections.
  connection_id?: string | null;
  // Parameters for the skill (must match skill_def.md schema)
  params: { [key: string]: unknown; };
  // API-opaque one-time bearer handle returned by execute_mutation_skill(confirm=false). Required when confirm=true; do not parse it or depend on its internal format.
  preview_token?: string | null;
  // Name of the mutation skill to execute
  skill_name: string;
}): Promise<CallToolResult<{
  connection_id?: string;
  db_type?: string;
  // Sanitized explanation on structured failures.
  error?: string;
  // Extensible machine-readable failure code. Published meanings are stable; unknown codes never authorize automatic retry.
  error_code?: string;
  // Database write conclusion. success describes tool handling; for a managed mutation this field describes the one framework-executed statement. Once an imperative callback runs, its whole-operation outcome remains unknown.
  execution_outcome: "not_executed" | "rolled_back" | "committed" | "unknown";
  idempotent?: boolean;
  mode: "preview" | "execute";
  // Business context from the Skill. For managed mutations, preview_sql and bound_params are generated by the framework from the cached plan and final preview binding.
  preview?: { [key: string]: unknown; };
  // API-opaque one-time bearer handle returned by preview and required for execute.
  preview_token?: string;
  preview_token_expires_at?: string;
  // Execution result; typically includes 'rowcount'. Shape is skill-defined.
  result?: { [key: string]: unknown; };
  skill_name: string;
  success: boolean;
  // Validation details when success=false (contains 'valid' and 'errors').
  validation?: { [key: string]: unknown; };
  [key: string]: unknown;
}>>; };
```

